{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-standard-ph-standard-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2af72ef92a5893e6549779546d86d6877538b007fb48e5776359eedc432de8dd", "source_text": "A standard ph covering is a standard V covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e0ece91e8df2994e63ed4477191da54175f34314e81c31f260218f9fd7c1c7e2", "unit_id": "tag:0ETD:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$f : U \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$U = \\bigcup_{j = 1, \\ldots, m} U_j$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_j \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$g : \\Spec(V) \\to T$", "MATH_0006": "$V$", "MATH_0007": "$K$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to T$", "MATH_0009": "$L/K$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(L) \\ar[rr] \\ar[d] & & U \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r] & \\Spec(V) \\ar[r]^g & T\n}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$W \\subset L$", "MATH_0012": "$V$", "MATH_0013": "$h$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(L) \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & \\Spec(W) \\ar[r]_h \\ar[d] & U \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r] & \\Spec(V) \\ar[r]^g & X\n}\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$\\Spec(W)$", "MATH_0016": "$\\Im(h)$", "MATH_0017": "$U_j$", "MATH_0018": "$j$", "MATH_0019": "$h : \\Spec(W) \\to U_j$", "MATH_0020": "$\\{U_j \\to T\\}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-standard-ph-covering}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-dominate}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-characterize-proper}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:823d7df1cb0e4ccda5b453c55dfd600750a8511a80a831ac3184535a7f96dac0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:67aee35343557f29c0196de9a8b1f41656baf191e4e6c2d20e8e4012965d60be", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a proper surjective\nmorphism. Let <MATH_0003> be a finite\naffine open covering. We have to show that <MATH_0004>\nis a standard V covering, see\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0005>\nbe a morphism where <MATH_0006> is a valuation ring with fraction field <MATH_0007>.\nSince <MATH_0008> is surjective, we may choose a field extension\n<MATH_0009> and a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0010>\nBy Algebra, Lemma <REF_0002> we can choose a valuation ring\n<MATH_0011> dominating <MATH_0012>. By the valuative criterion of\nproperness (Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0003>)\nwe can then find the morphism <MATH_0013> in the commutative\ndiagram\n<MATH_0014>\nSince <MATH_0015> has a unique closed point, we see that <MATH_0016>\nis contained in <MATH_0017> for some <MATH_0018>. Thus <MATH_0019>\nis the desired lift and we conclude <MATH_0020> is a standard V covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eef63df9ef7212c8afae40af67ebc9147cbb5e30c3eca3366fe02780378655a6", "unit_id": "tag:0ETD:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\{T_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T_j \\times_T T' \\to T'\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-standard-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:acacf1f5ffaeb9ff3d270b1b71c3cec98515804a0815dd5161e00949dc510c7c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:07d88a5620b927887028a1a8f1aafcf3eef5ba4ceb4ca8cafcc76b1149c28f79", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a standard V covering.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of affine schemes.\nThen <MATH_0003> is a\nstandard V covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f644dbd9f854649749511b45fa2a96209c3eaa13e7215c7e751a2825d7f2e97f", "unit_id": "tag:0ETE:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(V) \\to T'$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\subset W$", "MATH_0004": "$i$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(W) \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & T_i \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(V) \\ar[r] & T\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(W) \\to T' \\times_T T_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cf472698e170f3655487a3fea8c9690448ee78be3e8a7840a4cb788339a23c77", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5dd2d470174ef8ed547e1a056300bfa27bf2559d9e985869f359220283964262", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism where <MATH_0002> is a valuation ring.\nBy assumption we can find an extension of valuation rings <MATH_0003>,\nan <MATH_0004>, and a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0005>\nBy the universal property of fibre products\nwe obtain a morphism <MATH_0006>\nas desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9bd4c0e14316da6c0038c6e34ecd5564d6b276c0939638f9b794a52a71a934c5", "unit_id": "tag:0ETE:proof"}
